(7740824, 1276766, 83313, '<td valign="top">I find this fascinating. Your previous entry of this window scene fell a little short of a 6, while this one nailed a 7+ and the blue. Lighting was the same. I think the first one was actually the superior image, due to being zoomed in, it had a little more mystery about what the scene was about. That was in a freestudy, however, which we know people tend to vote a little more harshly on. Both shots got an 8 from me, because they received Grog comments. The grate one always gives an 8 as appreciation for inspiring a comment and letting him out of his cave for a while.<br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1275303" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img border="0" src="https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/3000-3999/3513/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1275303.jpg" xalt="'' . substr(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/3000-3999/3513/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1275303.jpg'', strrpos(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/3000-3999/3513/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1275303.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/></a></td>', 'I find this fascinating. Your previous entry of this window scene fell a little short of a 6, while this one nailed a 7+ and the blue. Lighting was the same. I think the first one was actually the superior image, due to being zoomed in, it had a little more mystery about what the scene was about. That was in a freestudy, however, which we know people tend to vote a little more harshly on. Both shots got an 8 from me, because they received Grog comments. The grate one always gives an 8 as appreciation for inspiring a comment and letting him out of his cave for a while.', '2023-03-27 01:18:23.000000', NULL, 0),
